#N canvas 20 20 2500 1860 12;
#X text 20 20 c_clock -- ONE clock. Not THE clock: Cut It runs poly-tempo \, so every grain engine \, sequencer and sampler that needs a beat owns an instance of this with its own rate and its own time signature. u_tempo is the master REFERENCE that instances may follow \, and nothing downstream may assume the global clock bus is its clock., f 58;
#X text 20 150 creation arg 1: the ratio to master tempo -- 1 follows it \, 1.5 runs half again as fast. creation arg 2: beats per bar. Both are corrected to 1 and 4 if they are nonsense \, and both say so on err. inlets: none. outlets \, left to right: the raw beat PHASE as a signal \, a beat bang \, the beat number within the bar \, and a bar bang., f 58;
#X obj 20 300 r tempo;
#X obj 20 345 *;
#X obj 200 300 r \$0-ratio;
#X obj 20 390 / 60;
#X obj 20 440 phasor~;
#X obj 20 500 outlet~;
