#X obj 2210 540 s err;
#X text 20 1300 THE x24 AND THE wrap~ ARE THE ALIGNMENT MECHANISM \, and they are the one thing in this file worth reading twice. A threshold at 0.5 of the BEAT phasor would fire half a beat away from u_tempo's beat \, because u_tempo's pulses fire at 0.5 of a PULSE. Multiplying by 24 and wrapping rebuilds u_tempo's exact construction off this instance's own phasor \, so two clocks at the same rate trigger in the same block -- by construction rather than by luck -- and a ratio of 1.5 diverges only because it is meant to., f 58;
#X text 20 1500 ONE PHASOR \, TWO USES. The signal outlet carries the beat phase for sample-accurate grain work \; the events are cut from the same ramp. A second oscillator at 24 times the rate would drift from the first \, slowly \, and only under a long take., f 58;
#X text 20 1630 A SIGNAL FAN-OUT NEEDS NO TRIGGER. Signal connections all run every block \, so there is no firing order to get wrong -- the trigger rule is about messages. Same note as u_root's level taps., f 58;
#X text 900 1300 START RESETS \, STOP DOES NOT HALT. A running phasor nobody reads is silent \, and halting it is the consumer's business -- the same reason u_tempo keeps sending clock while stopped. The start reset is the ONLY thing aligning instances to each other and to master \; after that \, equal frequencies from the same arithmetic hold the alignment on their own., f 44;
#X text 900 1480 FOUR RECEIVES ON ONE NAME \, and the order between them does not matter: all four write cold inlets and none of them fires anything. The phase goes to 0 \, threshold~ is forced low \, the pulse counter to 23 and the beat counter to beats-per-bar minus one -- so the NEXT pulse is pulse 0 of beat 1 of bar 1., f 44;
#X text 900 1660 THE BAR CHAIN RUNS BEFORE THE BEAT BANG. Values first \, event last: beat-in-bar and the bar bang are set from the right outlet \, and only then does the beat leave outlet 1. A consumer that reads beat-in-bar when the beat arrives gets this beat \, not the last one., f 44;
#X text 1660 660 BAD ARGUMENTS ARE CORRECTED IMMEDIATELY AND REPORTED LATE. The correction has to happen at load or the first tempo would drive a dead clock \; the warning waits 2 s because deploy.sh gates on OUTPUT and its check quits before then. Same trick as m_nano's channel print., f 44;
#X text 1660 840 moses' LEFT outlet carries the value it did not match \, as every reject in this repo does. It is harmless here only because its destination is a MESSAGE BOX \, which fires on anything -- put a trigger in front of it the moment that stops being true., f 44;
#X text 1660 1000 NO INSTANCES IN THE DEPLOYED PATCH. Nothing consumes a beat yet \, so u_root instantiates none of these \; tools/phase5-bench.pd makes two \, at ratios 1 and 1.5 \, which is what proves the poly part of poly-tempo., f 44;
